              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're asking how long do dry van trailers last, the honest answer is: it depends on how they're used and how well they're maintained. On average, a dry van trailer can last anywhere from 10 to 30 years, with many units staying on the road even longer when properly cared for. For owner-operators and fleet managers, that lifespan isn't just a number; it directly impacts your bottom line. The right trailer, backed by consistent trailer maintenance, can deliver years of dependable performance without unnecessary downtime.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-impacts",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Impacts the Lifespan of Dry Van Trailers?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "impacts"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-impacts-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not all dry van trailers age the same. Several factors determine how long your trailer will realistically last in day-to-day operations.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "features-impacts-2",
                  "type": "list",
                  "props": {
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "columns": 2,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Usage and Load Type",
                        "desc": "A trailer hauling lightweight, evenly distributed freight will naturally last longer than one carrying heavy or unbalanced loads. Constant strain on the flooring, axles, and suspension can shorten the lifespan over time."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Climate and Environment",
                        "desc": "Florida's heat, humidity, and exposure to road salt or coastal air can accelerate wear. Corrosion and moisture damage are common issues if trailers aren't properly maintained."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Build Quality",
                        "desc": "The materials and manufacturing behind a dry van trailer matter. Higher-quality construction often results in stronger structural integrity and longer service life."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Maintenance Routine",
                        "desc": "This is the biggest factor. Regular inspections, repairs, and preventative service can extend a trailer's life by years."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-how-old",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Old Should a Dry Van Trailer Be When You Buy It?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "how-old"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-how-old-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A common question we hear is: How old should a dry van trailer be? There's no one-size-fits-all answer, but here's a practical breakdown:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "stages-how-old-2",
                  "type": "stage-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "0–5 yrs",
                        "text": "Ideal for fleets that want reliability with minimal maintenance. Higher upfront cost, but fewer surprises."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "5–10 yrs",
                        "text": "A strong middle ground. With proper maintenance, these trailers still offer years of dependable use."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "10+ yrs",
                        "text": "More affordable, but condition matters. A well-maintained older trailer can still perform, but you'll want to inspect key components closely."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-how-old-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we help customers evaluate used inventory based on real-world conditions, not just age. That's how you avoid buying a trailer that looks good on paper but doesn't hold up on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-long-do-dry-van-trailers-last-in-real-use/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1000,
                      "height": 667,
                      "alt": "Sun State Leasing and Rental branding on the corner of a Hyundai Translead dry van trailer"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-signs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Signs Your Dry Van Trailer Is Reaching the End of Its Life",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "signs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Even the most dependable trailers eventually show signs of wear. Knowing what to look for helps you plan ahead instead of reacting to breakdowns.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-signs-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Structural Issues",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-signs-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Cracks in the frame"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Warping or weakening of the trailer body"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Roof or wall damage leading to leaks"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-signs-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Mechanical Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-signs-5",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Frequent brake or suspension issues"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Axle misalignment or tire wear patterns"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-6",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When repair costs start adding up and downtime becomes more frequent, it may be time to consider upgrading.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-maintenance",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Role of Trailer Maintenance in Longevity",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "maintenance"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-maintenance-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If there's one thing that determines how long dry van trailers last, it's maintenance. A consistent trailer maintenance plan should include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-maintenance-2",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Routine brake inspections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Tire checks and replacements"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Seal and roof inspections to prevent leaks"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Floor and structural evaluations"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lighting and electrical system checks"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-maintenance-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Staying ahead of small issues prevents larger, more expensive problems down the line. It also keeps your equipment compliant and your drivers safe. At Sun State Trailers, we've seen firsthand how a well-maintained trailer can outperform expectations year after year. It's not about pushing equipment to its limit; it's about taking care of it so it takes care of your business.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-long-do-dry-van-trailers-last-in-real-use/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1000,
                      "height": 667,
                      "alt": "Sun State International dealership building and wayfinding sign at the Tampa location"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-replace",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When It Makes Sense to Replace or Upgrade",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "replace"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-replace-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "There comes a point where continuing to repair a trailer costs more than replacing it. If you're experiencing:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-replace-2",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Frequent downtime"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Increasing repair costs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Missed deliveries due to equipment issues"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-replace-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "…it may be time to look at your options. This is where flexibility matters. Whether you're expanding your fleet or replacing aging equipment, having access to new, used, and rental trailers gives you the ability to make the right decision for your operation.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "links-replace-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "links-replace-4",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "marginTop": 8,
