                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-choosing-right-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The goal isn't just to buy a trailer. It's to invest in something that supports your business long-term. At Sun State Trailers, we take a straightforward approach: we help you find the right fit for your workload, we focus on dependable equipment that holds up over time, and we provide support so you're not left figuring things out on your own. That commitment comes from years of experience and a customer-first mindset.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "choosing-right"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-3",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-long-do-dry-van-trailers-last-in-real-use/3.jpg",
                      "width": 1000,
                      "height": 667,
                      "alt": "Close-up of a dry van trailer's landing gear and undercarriage detail"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-bottom-line",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Long Do Dry Van Trailers Last?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "bottom-line"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-bottom-line-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "So, how long do dry van trailers last in real use? With proper care, smart purchasing decisions, and consistent trailer maintenance, you can expect a dry van trailer to last well over a decade, sometimes closer to 30+ years. The difference comes down to how you manage it. If you're thinking about upgrading, expanding, or simply want to make sure you're getting the most out of your current equipment, <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a> is here to help you move forward with confidence.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
